e of the build pack that's where it  decides what language it is and it  should show us that yep it is using go  and  then it does the build it's going to  compile my go code  using go 114 and  it is doing that now looks like it just  finished  and now it's going to create my final  docker image uh putting my application  code  on top of the stack so it's doing that  and it looks like it is now putting the  completed image  into my container registry and that is  all done  so now that we have a built  container image let's deploy it  so to deploy it i'm going to use cloud  run that is google's  next generation serverless container  engine  and i'm just going to tell it to  deploy a new service to cloud run and  using that image that we  uh just created from cloud build  so i fire this up and it's going to ask  me a few questions i'm going to choose  our fully managed  cloud run platform you can of course  also  use um cloudrunforanthos  if you uh have installed that on top of  your anthos cluster  i haven't so i'm just going to choose  the fully managed option  and i'm going to call this my demo  run for  screencast service  that should be unique and i'll choose  the region let's go us central  and allow unauthenticated just to make  this more interesting  let's um just make this a private  service  that uh you need to be authenticated to  use so  i'm doing that and now it is deploying  the service  and um cloud run services have revisions  uh this will be the first revision  and now it's routing traffic to it so  we're all done  and it gives me this url right here  which i can use  to access the service and i  am going to hit that up i'm just going  to use the curl command right here so we  stay right in the terminal  and here's my command i'm curling that  same url  and you can see i'm adding a header with  an authorization field and then i'm  going to call the gcloud command again  to give it my identity token so i do  that  and it's firing it up and boom it  we 